  "body": "Closes #610 (with #739: scopes 1 and 3 there, scope 2 here)\nClaim: mac/m4-captures\n\n**Merge after #739.** This branch is stacked on `capture/610-mp-list-reply-order` (#739) and holds its commits until #739 lands. Once #739 is squashed, merge `dev-swift` into this branch, keep both MANIFEST blocks and both §6c bullets, and check that `git diff` shows only the group files.\n\n**Problem.** Scope 2 of #610: the MP list around a reply in a group conversation. The operator gave the go on 2026-11-10 for a four-member group with two other members, as in `W70`/`W73`.\n\n**What was captured** (Run 18). The two writes that reach the other members (`W610e` create, `W610g` reply) were sent by the main session; everything else by `mac/m4-captures`, between the two kit accounts, one request per minute.\n- **Setup:** user1 creates the four-member group `fixture-test-7` (`W610e`). user2 then sends `fixture-test-8` to user1 (`W610f`), so the group is row 2 in both lists (`R610e`, `R610f`).\n- **The reply:** user2, who is not the owner, replies once (`W610g`). In the creator's list the group row moves above the newer `fixture-test-8` and turns \"Nouveau message\" with 1 reply (`R610g`). In user2's own list it is row 1 (`R610h`).\n- **The `[non lu]` span:** in the creator's view, after the reply, it names the replier too.\n- **Cleanup:** both kit accounts deleted `fixture-test-8`. The group thread is kept, as agreed.\n\n**What changed.**\n- The captures, `corpus.json`, `MANIFEST.md` (Run 18) and HFR-PROTOCOL §6c LOT-140 (the group bullet replaces the pending mark).\n- `HopResponseParserTests.writeConfirmations` gains `W610e`-`W610g`: the corpus sweep requires every write confirmation to be listed. `swift test --package-path Packages/HFRKit` passes locally.\n\n**Leak check.** An independent Sonnet sub-agent found 0 real pseudos, titles, credentials, cookies or `hash_check`. The per-file aliases are consistent, and only already-public ids remain. `check --corpus` and `check --config --private` are clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
